   $q$According to the passage, what do "gently worn," "previously owned," and "used" have in common?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They all describe items that are brand new and still in their boxes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"They all refer to the same fact: someone else owned the item first.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They all describe clothing and cannot be used for other objects.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"They all describe items that are damaged and should not be bought.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralizes"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They all refer to the same fact: someone else owned the item first.$q$, $q$The first paragraph says each phrase "refers to the same plain fact: someone else had the item first." The passage applies them to sweaters, bicycles, and lamps, so they are not limited to clothing.$q$, 'draft', 'c715a5ec-fabf-5e3c-b191-c6859aba3332')
