   $q$Dad calls the breakdown "a minor crisis." Why does the narrator say this phrase "only made sense in our family"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Because the family speaks a language no one else understands.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Because \"minor\" and \"crisis\" clash, and the family uses such jokes to stay calm.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Because Dad was angry and wanted to blame someone for the problem.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"Because the breakdown was the worst thing that ever happened to them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because "minor" and "crisis" clash, and the family uses such jokes to stay calm.$q$, $q$A crisis is serious by definition, so "minor crisis" is a playful oxymoron that admits trouble while keeping things light, a habit the narrator links to the family. Nothing shows Dad was angry; he calmly opens the hood.$q$, 'draft', 'b529d6f7-7092-5e3d-9d11-a9c17f8c195f')
