  ('5792480a-d71f-511a-a663-ede924ada13e', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The final paragraph says the octopus's skin "turns that weakness into" a survival tool. What is the effect of this wording?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It proves that the octopus is the strongest predator in the sea.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates"},{"text":"It warns readers that octopuses are too weak to survive for long.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"It suggests the octopus will grow a shell as it gets older.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It shows that the soft body, which seems like a flaw, is linked to its greatest strength.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows that the soft body, which seems like a flaw, is linked to its greatest strength.$q$, $q$The wording sets up a contrast: a soft, "boneless body might seem like a weakness," yet the flexible skin makes it "one of the most impressive survival tools." The passage never calls the octopus a top predator; it says it has "very few defenses."$q$, 'draft', '722083c6-6b19-5207-9ec3-f9fcc6af7d55')
