  ('1d4eedff-e373-56b7-9668-919114058db3', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Critics called cyclists "a nuisance." Which word, if used instead, would make the critics sound even harsher?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"trend,\" which suggests something many people are trying","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-connotation"},{"text":"\"pastime,\" which suggests a pleasant way to spend free time","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-connotation"},{"text":"\"menace,\" which suggests a real threat to people's safety","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"novelty,\" which suggests something new and interesting","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-connotation"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"menace," which suggests a real threat to people's safety$q$, $q$"Nuisance" means an annoyance, and "menace" moves the same complaint further toward danger, so it would sound harsher. "Novelty," "pastime," and "trend" are neutral or positive, so they would soften the criticism instead.$q$, 'draft', '21297116-8a38-59cf-b06a-e1d983fd9485')
