  ('ffdfc23d-e225-5057-b26d-1a654d9a6f72', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The narrator says words were "tools too, as useful as the box cutter, and just as easy to use carelessly." What does this comparison suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Words can help when used well, but they can also cause harm if chosen without care.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Words matter less than the physical tools a store worker uses.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"Ms. Petrakis is careless with both her words and her tools.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Workers should use the box cutter to open boxes of words.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Words can help when used well, but they can also cause harm if chosen without care.$q$, $q$A box cutter is useful but can hurt someone if handled carelessly, and the narrator applies the same idea to word choice after watching Ms. Petrakis calm the customer. The comparison says words are "as useful as" the tool, not less important.$q$, 'draft', 'd9955455-305e-502d-934b-7b6201903b64')
