   $q$By dinner, "the word had grown in his mind like a weed." What does this simile suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Jun's worry about the text kept spreading the more he thought about it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Jun believed Marisol had sent him a message about plants.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-target"},{"text":"Jun was planning to help his family with gardening after dinner.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Jun had forgotten about the text completely by dinnertime.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Jun's worry about the text kept spreading the more he thought about it.$q$, $q$Weeds spread quickly and are hard to get rid of, just as Jun's worry kept growing until he spent "an hour drafting a reply." He clearly had not forgotten the text.$q$, 'draft', 'c639ac32-73f1-5922-9044-9b583b0e2340')
