   $q$Hana says, "That period is cold." What does she mean by calling the period "cold"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Marisol must have typed the message outside in winter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The period was typed by mistake and has no meaning at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The period makes the message sound unfriendly or distant.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The period makes the message sound excited and cheerful.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The period makes the message sound unfriendly or distant.$q$, $q$"Cold" here describes tone, and Hana explains that "a period ends a conversation," which makes the reply feel unfriendly. She contrasts it with an exclamation point, which would sound warmer and more cheerful.$q$, 'draft', 'c639ac32-73f1-5922-9044-9b583b0e2340')
