  ('4222c118-beb0-50c0-948a-627cc6101506', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-figurative-language'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Jun says "Fine." felt "like a door closing quietly but firmly." What does this description suggest about how he read the message?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He thought Marisol was shouting at him in anger.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates"},{"text":"He thought Marisol was calmly but clearly ending the discussion.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He thought the message was warm and welcoming.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"He thought Marisol was inviting him over to her house.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He thought Marisol was calmly but clearly ending the discussion.$q$, $q$A door closing "quietly but firmly" is not loud, yet it is final, which matches Jun's fear that Marisol was politely shutting him out. The word "quietly" rules out reading it as shouting.$q$, 'draft', 'c639ac32-73f1-5922-9044-9b583b0e2340')
