   $q$The author calls the migration "an astonishing feat" for an insect that "weighs less than a paper clip." What is the purpose of this contrast?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To argue that monarchs are heavier than most other insects.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-target"},{"text":"To emphasize how impressive a long journey is for such a tiny creature.","is_correct":true},{"text":"To suggest that the journey is easy because the butterflies are light.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"To explain that monarchs carry paper clips during their migration.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To emphasize how impressive a long journey is for such a tiny creature.$q$, $q$Setting a tiny weight beside a trip of "more than two thousand miles" makes the journey seem even more amazing, which fits the word "astonishing." The contrast stresses difficulty, not ease.$q$, 'draft', '29d9d21a-0815-5fb6-9f1c-6aad492f292c')
