values
  ('2243de29-74b5-5993-9663-b62f2b110028', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Some scientists call the population "fragile," while others use the stronger word "endangered." What is the difference between these two words?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The two words mean exactly the same thing, so the scientists fully agree.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-connotation"},{"text":"\"Fragile\" means the butterflies break easily when touched, while \"endangered\" means they are safe.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"\"Fragile\" suggests the population could be easily harmed, while \"endangered\" signals a serious risk of disappearing.","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"Fragile\" means the numbers are growing, while \"endangered\" means they are falling.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-denotation"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Fragile" suggests the population could be easily harmed, while "endangered" signals a serious risk of disappearing.$q$, $q$Both words describe a population at risk, but the author calls "endangered" "the stronger word," pointing to a more urgent threat of disappearing. The scientists do not fully agree, since they choose different words.$q$, 'draft', '29d9d21a-0815-5fb6-9f1c-6aad492f292c')
